'''Pataxó''' (Patashó, sometimes called Southern Pataxó to distinguish from [[Pataxó-Hãhãhãe language|Pataxó-Hãhãhãe]]) is an [[extinct language|extinct]] [[Maxakalían languages|Maxakalían]] language of [[Brazil]]<ref name="Nikulin-Macro-Je">{{Cite web |last=Nikulin |first=Andrey |title=Proto-Macro-Jê: um estudo reconstrutivo |url=http://etnolinguistica.org/local--files/tese%3Anikulin-2020/Nikulin_2020_Proto-Macro-Je.pdf |website=etnolinguistica.org}}</ref> formerly spoken by the [[Pataxó people]] of the [[Bahia]] region, and of [[Minas Gerais]], Pôsto Paraguassu in [[Itabuna]] municipality. The 12,865 individuals in the [[Pataxó]] tribe now speak [[Portuguese language|Portuguese]] instead, though they retain a few Pataxó words, as well as some words from neighbouring peoples.<ref name=":0" /> It has been revived in a form called Patxohã.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Bomfim |first=Anari |last2=Lima |first2=Suzi |date=2020-10-01 |title=Count and mass nouns in Patxohã |url=http://www.jbe-platform.com/content/journals/10.1075/lv.00024.bom |journal=Linguistic Variation |language=en |volume=20 |issue=2 |pages=324–335 |doi=10.1075/lv.00024.bom |issn=2211-6834|url-access=subscription }}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Nelson |first=Jessica Fae |date=2023-10-01 |title=On Pataxó Hãhãhãe and Maxakalí |url=https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/10.1086/726150 |journal=International Journal of American Linguistics |language=en |volume=89 |issue=4 |pages=531–563 |doi=10.1086/726150 |issn=0020-7071|url-access=subscription }}</ref> Due to poor documentation, many elements of Pataxó grammar, including the entire syntax, needed to be entirely reconstructed.<ref name="Nikulin-Macro-Je" />

